# Implement structured logging

- Source URL: https://github.com/UTOSS/risc-v/issues/60

As the core gets bigger and more complicated, VCD diagrams will become harder to read especially at the top level. I think it would be good to have some sort of logging capability built into processor at least during development stages so that we can get diagnose issues more easily.

Example of logging that I saw that our reference model for RISCOF has log callbacks set up here: https://github.com/riscv/sail-riscv/blob/cbddfcd979ba6ad4e2c5abbacb20636e3e1f4916/c_emulator/riscv_callbacks_log.cpp and the logs themselves look like something like
```
...
[3] [M]: 0x0000100C (0x0182A283) lw t0, 0x18(t0)
mem[R,0b0000000000000000000001000000011000] -> 0x80000000
x5 <- 0x80000000
mem[X,0b0000000000000000000001000000010000] -> 0x8067
mem[X,0b0000000000000000000001000000010010] -> 0x0002
[4] [M]: 0x00001010 (0x00028067) jalr zero, 0x0(t0)
mem[X,0b0010000000000000000000000000000000] -> 0x0837
mem[X,0b0010000000000000000000000000000010] -> 0x7D5C
...
```

RISC-V also has a draft for a "verification interface" that defines similar attributes for traces (i.e. writing to mem/registers, current instruction, etc.): https://github.com/riscv-verification/RVVI
